Skip same-value draw.end in an instance loop and vertex_buffer.first/count on the split front.
Port of zortos293/Eglantine 7e2a9fe (split-front part; UsageTracker is already here). The front still
sent writes the back ignores: draw.end while the draw manager is in DrawMode::Instance (DrawEnd
draws nothing), and vertex_buffer.first/count with an unchanged value (they flush no deferred draw
and are only read by the draw manager). FrontState tracks the instance loop from draw.begin's
instance id (First leaves, Subsequent enters) and clears it on inline index methods; the multi-word
path tracks every word, like the back's per-word DrawBegin, and uses the replayed value. Only with
skip_same and an unchanged shadow; index_buffer.first/count are never skipped (they mark the index
buffer dirty). The non-split CallMethod path is unchanged. Upstream's FPS figure is not measured here.
